  "term": "psychoanalyst",
  "definition": "A psychoanalyst is a healthcare professional who uses psychoanalysis to help people work through difficulties and create lasting change in their lives. Practitioners from several professions may serve in this role, including psychiatrists, psychologists, nurse practitioners, social workers, counselors, and marriage and family therapists.",
